WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:05.500
Before we understand what polynomials are,

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:09.700
let's look at the concept of terms and expressions!

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.180
14xz Plus 53y Minus 3.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:17.720
There is a plus as well as a minus sign here,

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.700
which means that we have three terms.

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:25.120
14xz, 53y and 3.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:30.000
The second expression is '23x squared y' minus

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:31.960
'4y cubed'.

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:35.100
This expression has just two terms.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:39.200
'23x squared y' and '4y cubed'.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.420
Now we can move on to understanding

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:45.460
the most important concept in algebraic expressions.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:48.320
It's the concept of polynomials.

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:53.020
As you can see the word has been colored into two parts.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:54.980
Poly means Many.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:01:00.900
And nomial means parts or terms in the case of algebraic expressions.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:04.960
And that's how the word polynomial comes about.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:07.840
There are different types of polynomials.

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:12.120
A polynomial can be an expression with just one term,

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:14.020
or two terms,

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:18.720
or three terms, or maybe even a greater number of terms.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:24.360
All these categories come under one roof which is the polynomial.

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:26.660
Expressions with just one term ,

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:30.880
two terms, or three terms are given special names.

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:34.700
An expression with one term is called Monomial .

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:38.840
An expression with two terms is called a binomial.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:43.700
And an expression that has 3 terms is called a  trinomial.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:49.920
Mono is one, Bi is two at Tri is three.

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:52.700
There is a common misconception that only

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:56.540
an expression with more than three terms is called a polynomial.

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:58.660
That's incorrect!

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:03.980
All expression which have one or more terms are called  polynomials!

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:06.860
Let's look at a few examples of each.

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:11.620
The number seven is a Monomial. It's just one term.

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:14.700
4x is also a Monomial.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:19.180
It's just one term as 'four' and 'x' are multiplied.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:23.080
Even '3ab squared' is a Monomial.

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:26.040
And yes, all these expressions are also

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:28.320
polynomials.

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:32.160
An example of a binomial would be '4 plus x'.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:35.640
The plus sign separates the terms.

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:40.320
Another example would be '3xy' minus 'x'.

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:45.560
An Example of a Trinomial would be '3' plus 'a' plus 'b'.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:50.240
It has three terms one, two and three.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:54.600
Or maybe '3cd' plus 'a' plus '8'.

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:56.980
Again, let me remind you,

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:01.180
all these examples you have seen are polynomials.

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:08.340
And an example of the last type would be '4z' plus '9' plus '3x' plus 'y'.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:10.720
It has four terms in all.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:17.440
So remember, a polynomial is an expression which has one or more terms.

